* rt_xuser.cal: run short user programs from an X-MP test in monitor mode.
* Include after rt_xmp.cal.  As rt_user.cal, with the X-MP form of the
* exchange package.  The test must define
*
*     UPKG       word address of the user exchange package (a multiple of 20)
*
* and may set, before the first UGO, the words the package is built from:
*
*     U$W1       word 1: instruction base address and the mode bits of word 1
*     U$W2       word 2: instruction limit address and the mode bits of word 2
*     U$W4       word 4: data base address, program state, cluster number
*     U$W5       word 5: data limit address
*
* UDATA gives them these values: both fields from word 0 to the end of
* memory, operand range and floating point interrupts off, cluster 0.  A
* test changes one by storing into it.
*
* UGO KP1 writes a fresh package at UPKG (P from the word KP1, the four
* words above, exchange address back to UPKG, everything else zero) and
* exchanges to it.  The test goes on behind the UGO when the program exits
* or is interrupted; UPKG then holds the program's package.
*
* UFLAG Sr leaves the nine flags of bits 31 to 39 of that package in Sr.
*
         MACRO   UGO %KP
         U$S7,0  S7
         U$A7,0  A7
         S7      %KP,0
         UPKG,0  S7
         S7      U$W1,0
         UPKG+1,0 S7
         S7      U$W2,0
         UPKG+2,0 S7
         S7      U$W3,0
         UPKG+3,0 S7
         S7      U$W4,0
         UPKG+4,0 S7
         S7      U$W5,0
         UPKG+5,0 S7
         A7      UPKG
         XA      A7
         S7      U$S7,0
         A7      U$A7,0
         EX
         ENDM
         MACRO   UFLAG %REG
         %REG    UPKG+3,0
         %REG    %REG<D'31               ; F is bits 31 to 39 from the left
         %REG    %REG>D'55
         ENDM
         MACRO   UDATA
U$S7     CON     0
U$A7     CON     0
U$W1     CON     0
U$W2     CON     T$XLMAX*T$P2_29
U$W3     CON     UPKG/20*T$P2_40
U$W4     CON     0
U$W5     CON     T$XLMAX*T$P2_29
         ENDM
